    "state": "Subject: This is not the way to treat a guest\n\nFrom: Beatriz Okafor\nTo: Bracken Quay Hotel\n\nI am writing because my stay in room 418 was miserable, and I am tired of being passed from one department to another. I checked in on Tuesday afternoon for two nights. The desk clerk was polite, but the room was noisy, and the restaurant staff seemed unable to coordinate a simple meal. I want the hotel to take the complaint seriously instead of sending me another cheerful survey invitation.\n\nFrom: Bracken Quay Hotel Guest Services\nTo: Beatriz Okafor\n\nWe are sorry that you found the room noisy. Our records show that a maintenance worker visited at 9:15 p.m. after you reported a rattling vent. He tightened a loose panel, and the noise stopped. That repair does not address your separate complaint about dinner. We have asked the restaurant manager to review the ticket and will follow up.\n\nFrom: Beatriz Okafor\nTo: Bracken Quay Hotel Guest Services\n\nThe repair helped, but nobody needs to congratulate themselves for fixing a rattling vent. At dinner I ordered the mushroom risotto and sparkling water. The server brought tomato soup instead. I pointed out that it was the wrong dish, and the server took it away. I waited another thirty-five minutes for the risotto. It was lukewarm when it finally arrived. I did not order the roast chicken, despite the note on the kitchen docket saying “chicken—table 14.” That was another guest’s meal, not mine.\n\nI am not asking you to comp my room, and I am not requesting money back for the dinner. Please do not treat those as things I asked for just because guests sometimes do. I want a written apology from the restaurant manager and an explanation of how a wrong dish and such a long delay happened. I also want the hotel to stop telling me that the kitchen was busy; I can see that the kitchen was busy from the timestamps, and it is not an explanation for handing me someone else’s order.\n\nFrom: Bracken Quay Hotel Restaurant Manager\nTo: Beatriz Okafor\n\nI reviewed the ticket history. The soup was entered under your table by mistake. The chicken belonged to table 14, whose guests also reported a delay, but their order is unrelated to your account. Your risotto ticket was delayed after the first dish was voided. I am sorry that the meal was not served promptly or at the proper temperature. The restaurant will brief the team on checking table numbers before food leaves the pass.\n\nFrom: Beatriz Okafor\nTo: Bracken Quay Hotel Restaurant Manager\n\nThat is at least an answer, although “brief the team” sounds like the sort of promise that disappears by tomorrow. I am still angry that I had to chase you to get a response. Please confirm that the written apology will come from the manager, not an automated message. Again, I have not asked for compensation. My complaint is about the service and the lack of a timely response, not a demand for cash. I want an actual person to acknowledge it.\n\nFrom: Bracken Quay Hotel Guest Services\nTo: Beatriz Okafor\n\nConfirmed: the restaurant manager has sent the apology in this thread. We have also recorded your request for a written explanation. Your room charge remains unchanged because you did not request a room refund or a discount. We are sorry the stay fell short of your expectations, and we will not send the survey invitation you mentioned.\n\nFrom: Beatriz Okafor\nTo: Bracken Quay Hotel Guest Services\n\nI have received the apology. I still think the hotel handled this badly, and I expect you to make sure future guests are not served a dish ordered by somebody else. Please do not confuse my request for an explanation with a request for a refund. I have said plainly that I am not asking for money back.",
