    "state": "Cedar Steps School, evening office desk — typed copy of a handwritten page from the blue attendance notebook. The original was written in a hurry between two bell rings; there are arrows, a coffee ring, and a line that trails off. The person who typed it says she kept the rambling parts because the short version looked like it could mean something else. Name at the top: Aiden Fischer. Course: Sound and Story Workshop. Date of note: 6 September.\n\nI talked to the office yesterday, and I want to make sure this isn't put down as “asked about class” and then forgotten. I am asking to leave the sound walk and the editing lab. Those are the two parts I cannot attend anymore. I want to stay in the listening circle, which is the third part, because that one still works with my schedule. Please don't mark all three parts as gone just because the course name is one title. The form has three little boxes, and I mean the first and third boxes as printed on my copy: sound walk and editing lab. The listening circle box should remain checked.\n\nI know I asked last week, “Could I possibly stop the editing lab if my shift changes?” That was only a question about what might happen. My shift did change yesterday, so this note is the actual request. It is not only about the editing lab anymore; I am asking for sound walk too because the transportation home was changed. The bus route note on the noticeboard says the 8:10 bus is delayed on Thursdays, but my sound walk is on Wednesday. The route note is not the reason the whole course is ending; it is just one of the scraps pinned near the sign-up sheet.\n\nThe fee sheet says sound walk is 70 credits, editing lab is 80, and listening circle is 50. The total is 200 credits. I see a handwritten calculation on the margin that says 70 + 80 = 160, which is wrong; it should be 150. The extra 10 in the margin is from somebody adding a late-registration charge that is not on my account. I paid 200 for all three parts, not 210. I a