    "state": "Westmere School of Applied Languages — registrar's monthly service report, forwarded with a handwritten cover note that has been typed up. Prepared by Xiu Rahman for the internal admin meeting. Tone of original note: “I know, I know, this is more detail than anyone asked for, but the attendance register and the booking screen disagree in three places, and I would rather explain it now than have someone chase the wrong student later.” The report concerns the course Practical Translation Clinic, which has four separately recorded components: intake seminar, paired translation, terminology lab, and final review. Students often call all four “the clinic.”\n\nCurrent class status, checked against the room log at 3:40 p.m.: intake seminar met on 2 November, paired translation met on 9 November, terminology lab is scheduled for 16 November, and final review is scheduled for 23 November. No component has been cancelled. A draft timetable on the staff printer lists final review on 24 November, but the signed timetable and student portal both say 23 November. The extra day in the draft came from an earlier room-hire discussion and should not be treated as the current date. Two students asked whether the clinic was cancelled when the corridor was closed for painting; the room was moved down one floor and the sessions proceeded.\n\nOne message in the shared inbox came from Rosa Moreau, a registered student. She wrote: “Please remove me from paired translation, terminology lab, and final review. I want to keep the intake seminar because I already attended it and need the notes.” This is the clearest line in the thread, and the action list in her account has those three requested component withdrawals. Her next sentence asks whether any fees can be credited and whether she should return her workbook. Those are questions, not additional withdrawal requests. The workbook is checked out to her and has not been returned, but that fact does not change the list of request