    "state": "Foxglove Dental — web form submission copied with staff comments\n\nSubmission received through the Foxglove Dental vendor-portal form. The form is used for contract notices, payment questions, and requests for documents; choosing a topic does not itself settle a legal issue. The person submitting is Greta Sorensen, the practice administrator. The other named party is Lumen Ledger Services, a fictional billing contractor. Greta uploaded the signed service schedule and the monthly invoice. The portal export has included the submitter's wording, a few auto-filled fields, and staff comments, because apparently one clean page would be too much to ask.\n\nSelected topic: “Contract charge dispute.”\nAgreement reference: LL-44, signed by both parties on April 1, 2026.\nMonthly service fee: $1,250.\nOptional paper-record storage: $90 per month, selected in writing.\nOne-time onboarding fee: $200, charged only in the first month.\nInvoice period: May 1 through May 31.\nInvoice line items: monthly service $1,250; paper storage $90; onboarding $200; expedited delivery $45; total before tax $1,585.\nPayment status: Foxglove has paid $1,340 for this invoice, covering the $1,250 monthly service and $90 storage. The onboarding fee was paid on the April invoice and is not payable again. Expedited delivery was not ordered or performed.\n\nThe agreement says a customer may dispute a charge for a service that was not ordered or performed. A successful dispute removes only that charge from the current invoice. It does not create a refund for another invoice, and the customer must still pay all other correctly invoiced amounts. A dispute is timely if submitted within 20 calendar days after the invoice date. The invoice date is May 2, 2026. The portal records submission on May 21, 2026, at 4:45 p.m. The contract says to count the day after the invoice date as day one and include the submission day. Weekends count as calendar days; there is no special holiday extension.\n\nA