    "state": "Incident postmortem — Northwind Analytics, search degradation. On 8 June, the team deployed a new indexer. For roughly 14 minutes, search results omitted recently added folders in some workspaces, while older folders remained searchable. The status page stayed green because its check tested only whether the search endpoint answered, not whether results were complete. No customer files were deleted, and the database showed no corruption. Ines Kowalski, the incident lead, initially suspected a permissions regression; the access audit later showed permissions were unchanged. The actual trigger was a schema mismatch between the indexer and one shard. Restarting the indexer alone did not help. The team rolled back the deployment, rebuilt the affected shard, and verified that new folders appeared in search. A separate spike in login latency began the previous evening and was traced to a scheduled analytics job; it was unrelated to this incident and ended before the search deployment. The postmortem recommends a result-completeness check and shard-schema validation before release. Both are recommendations, not completed controls. The timeline calls the event 'a wonderfully selective search experience,' which is not a product feature.",
