g entries should be checked against final job status. Account management will send Bluefin Dental a measured explanation of the delay and final delivery. The incident coordinator will keep the sandbox test in the engineering appendix while excluding it from production customer counts. I will review the next draft of the summary and ask that customer names remain next to their own verified facts.\n\nClosing. Thank you for reviewing the account distinctions with care. It is tempting to use the incident headline as a shortcut, but the headline covers several related investigations and is not itself a customer-level finding. In particular, please do not transfer Bluefin Dental’s retry symptom to Kestrel Supply. Kestrel’s own delivery record and its later confirmation both show that the scheduled file was delivered at the expected time. The report should reflect that evidence even though the initial subject line used the words “missing payment export.”",
