    "state": "Incident postmortem — Harbor Analytics developer platform\n\nWith sincere apologies for the lengthy update, we are documenting Tuesday’s CI notification issue. At 13:05 the pipeline service began sending duplicate messages to the team channel whenever a build entered the waiting state. The actual build queue continued to process jobs normally. The messages made the dashboard seem busier than it was, but they did not create extra builds or change job results.\n\nThe notification rule had been copied from a test configuration and subscribed to both the queue event and the status-refresh event. Those two events were emitted for the same waiting job, so the alert service posted twice. We checked the compiler and test-runner logs; neither showed an error associated with the duplicate alerts. A separate dependency warning appeared in one unrelated branch, but the branch owner resolved it before this incident began.\n\nAt 13:22, Hiro Mensah compared the message timestamps and identified that each pair had the same build identifier and different event identifiers. At 13:41, the on-call engineer removed the extra subscription. At 14:02, a new waiting job produced one notification, and the team confirmed the correction. All builds that had been waiting continued afterward, and the release pipeline remained available.\n\nWe are grateful for the calm reports from the teams affected. No customer-facing service interruption was recorded. No build was lost, no test failure was introduced by the notification rule, and no duplicate deployment took place. The alert configuration change is complete. The platform group will add a duplicate-event check to its notification tests and review other copied rules next week. That review is planned, not completed. Please accept our thanks for your patience and our apologies for the unnecessary messages.",
